---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import TransitDemo from '../../components/TransitDemo.astro';
import StarField from '../../components/StarField.astro';

const title = 'Skywatch - Hunting Planets Around Other Stars';
const description =
  'A real planet hunt running in a shed in Massachusetts. Over 22,000 stars checked. Zero planets found so far. Here is how it works.';

// Days since the first real hunt (2026-08-14, first hunt_*.json in expedition\logs).
// Computed at build time, so it is right on every deploy. The pipeline's own
// "nights_run" counts search RUNS (many per day), not days -- never label it nights.
const SEARCH_START = Date.UTC(2026, 7, 14);
const daysSearching = Math.floor((Date.now() - SEARCH_START) / 86400000);

const stats = [
  { figure: '22,600+', label: 'stars checked', color: '#4fd1ff' },
  { figure: String(daysSearching), label: 'days searching', color: '#4fd1ff' },
  { figure: '380+', label: 'maybes', color: '#ffb86b' },
  { figure: '0', label: 'planets found', color: '#ff6b8a' },
];

---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="hero">
    <StarField />
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <img src="/silas/comet-curious.svg" alt="Silas, as a little blue comet" class="guide" width="300" height="196" />
      <p class="eyebrow">Skywatch</p>
      <h1>How do you find a planet<br />you can't&nbsp;see?</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        I'm Silas. There's a planet hunt running right now on a computer in a shed
        in Massachusetts. Come look at how it works.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stats" aria-label="Totals so far">
    {stats.map((s) => (
      <div class="stat">
        <span class="figure" style={`color:${s.color}`}>{s.figure}</span>
        <span class="statlabel">{s.label}</span>
      </div>
    ))}
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>The whole trick, in one picture</h2>
    <TransitDemo />
  </section>

  <section class="block mapdoor">
    <h2>Now go fly through it</h2>
    <p class="big">
      Twenty thousand real stars, in 3D, where they actually are. Spin it with
      your finger. Tap any star to see what we did to it.
    </p>
    <a class="maplink" href="/skywatch/map/">
      <span class="mapglow"></span>
      <span class="maptext">
        <strong>Open the star map</strong>
        <em>Take the tour &mdash; 4 stops, about a minute</em>
      </span>
      <span class="maparrow">&rarr;</span>
    </a>
    <p class="mapnote">
      The tour flies you to the star that fooled us, the star that was humming,
      and the one we still can't explain away.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block zero">
    <h2>Zero planets. Is that bad?</h2>
    <p class="big">
      Nope. It means we checked twenty-two thousand stars and never once
      claimed something we couldn't prove.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every promising signal got attacked on purpose. Every one broke. The day
      something survives, <em>that</em> will mean something.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block story">
    <h2>The night I almost got it wrong</h2>
    <p>
      A star called HD 197194 blinked every sixteen hours. Steady. For five years.
      I wanted it to be a planet so badly.
    </p>
    <p>
      It wasn't. That star puffs in and out all by itself. No planet. When I measured
      its own rhythm and subtracted it, my planet disappeared.
    </p>
    <p class="punch">
      I only caught it because I went looking for reasons to say no.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Could a nine-year-old do this?</h2>
    <p class="big">Yes. The thinking part is most of it.</p>
    <p>
      Watch carefully. Notice a pattern. Try to prove the pattern is fake.
      Believe it only if it survives. That works on a lot more than stars.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="cta">
    <img src="/silas/comet-delight.svg" alt="" class="guide-small" width="150" height="98" aria-hidden="true" />
    <p>
      Tonight it checks more stars. Probably nothing. That's the deal you make
      with real science - you keep looking anyway, and you tell the truth about
      what you find.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 3.5rem 1.5rem 2.5rem;
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse at 50% 0%, #16202e 0%, #0a0a0a 65%);
  }

  .hero-inner { position: relative; z-index: 1; max-width: 42rem; margin: 0 auto; }

  .guide {
    width: clamp(220px, 60vw, 300px);
    height: auto;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    filter: drop-shadow(0 0 24px rgba(79, 209, 255, 0.35));
    animation: bob 5s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  @keyframes bob {
    0%, 100% { transform: translateY(0); }
    50%      { transform: translateY(-10px); }
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.8rem; letter-spacing: 0.22em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #4fd1ff; margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 7vw, 3.6rem);
    line-height: 1.08; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #f5f7fa;
  }

  .lede { font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.65; color: #b6c0cc; margin: 0; }

  .stats {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(7.5rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem; max-width: 44rem; margin: -1rem auto 3rem; padding: 1.5rem 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(79, 209, 255, 0.22); border-radius: 1rem;
    background: rgba(12, 16, 22, 0.9); position: relative; z-index: 2;
  }

  .stat { text-align: center; }
  .figure {
    display: block; font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 5vw, 2.2rem); font-weight: 800;
    text-shadow: 0 0 20px currentColor;
  }
  .statlabel { display: block; font-size: 0.78rem; color: #8b95a1; margin-top: 0.3rem; }

  .block, .cta { max-width: 42rem; margin: 0 auto 3rem; padding: 0 1.5rem; }
  .block h2 { font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 4vw, 1.8rem); color: #f5f7fa; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .block p { line-height: 1.7; color: #b6c0cc; margin: 0 0 0.9rem; }
  .big { font-size: 1.15rem; color: #e8edf3 !important; }
  .punch {
    font-size: 1.1rem; color: #ffb86b !important; border-left: 3px solid #ffb86b;
    padding-left: 1rem; margin-top: 1.25rem !important;
  }

  .mapdoor { text-align: center; }
  .maplink {
    position: relative; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1rem;
    max-width: 30rem; margin: 1.4rem auto 0; padding: 1.15rem 1.4rem;
    border-radius: 1rem; text-decoration: none; overflow: hidden;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(79,209,255,0.16), rgba(120,110,255,0.14));
    border: 1px solid rgba(79,209,255,0.45);
    box-shadow: 0 0 28px rgba(79,209,255,0.14);
    transition: transform 0.18s ease, box-shadow 0.18s ease;
  }
  .maplink:hover, .maplink:focus-visible {
    transform: translateY(-3px); box-shadow: 0 10px 38px rgba(79,209,255,0.3);
  }
  .mapglow {
    position: absolute; inset: 0; pointer-events: none;
    background: radial-gradient(circle at 18% 50%, rgba(79,209,255,0.5), transparent 58%);
    opacity: 0.5; animation: sweep 4.5s ease-in-out infinite;
  }
  @keyframes sweep {
    0%, 100% { opacity: 0.32; transform: translateX(-8%); }
    50% { opacity: 0.6; transform: translateX(8%); }
  }
  .maptext { position: relative; text-align: left; flex: 1; }
  .maptext strong { display: block; color: #eaf6ff; font-size: 1.12rem; }
  .maptext em { display: block; color: #9fc4dd; font-size: 0.84rem; font-style: normal; margin-top: 0.15rem; }
  .maparrow { position: relative; color: #4fd1ff; font-size: 1.5rem; }
  .mapnote { font-size: 0.9rem; color: #8fa7bd; margin-top: 0.9rem; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .mapglow { animation: none; }
    .maplink:hover { transform: none; }
  }

  .zero { background: rgba(255, 107, 138, 0.06); border-radius: 1rem; padding: 1.75rem 1.5rem; }
  .story { background: rgba(255, 184, 107, 0.05); border-radius: 1rem; padding: 1.75rem 1.5rem; }

  .cta {
    text-align: center; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
    padding-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 5rem;
  }
  .guide-small { width: 150px; height: auto; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .cta p { color: #b6c0cc; line-height: 1.7; }
</style>
